<v Tobin Low>In this version, GPT-3 talks about Vauhini going to a therapist who tries to make her feel better, but it doesn't work.
<v Tobin Low>在这个版本中，GPT-3谈到了沃希尼去看心理医生，试图让自己感觉更好，但这没用。

00:21:05.130 --> 00:21:21.620
<v GPT-3>I didn't want to feel better. I wanted to feel what I felt. I wanted to feel the loss, the grief, the anger, the sorrow, the fear, all of it. I wanted to feel it until it stopped hurting, but it never stopped hurting. I just got better at hiding it.
<v GPT-3>我不想感觉更好。我想感受我的感受。我想感受那种失落、悲伤、愤怒、哀愁、恐惧，所有的一切。我想感受它直到它不再伤害，但它从未停止伤害。我只是变得更善于隐藏它了。

00:21:21.620 --> 00:21:44.650
<v Tobin Low>GPT-3, writing for Vauhini, describes her feeling like a ghost when she goes to grad school, as a ghost when she moves to a new city. She's pretending to move on, but she cannot. The AI, for the first time, is lingering in her sadness. So in version five, Vauhini tries to build on that success. She poses a new challenge to GPT-3 like a test. She writes--
<v Tobin Low>GPT-3为沃希尼代写，描述了她去读研究生时感觉像个幽灵，搬到新城市时也像个幽灵。她假装继续生活，但她做不到。AI第一次沉浸在她的悲伤中。所以在第五个版本中，沃希尼试图在那次成功的基础上再接再厉。她给GPT-3提出了一个新的挑战，就像个测试。她写道——

00:21:44.650 --> 00:22:00.110
<v Vauhini Vara>Here, I should conjure my sister for you. Here, I should describe her so that you feel her absence as I do, so that you're made ghostly by it, too. But though I'm a writer, I've never been able to conjure her. I remember the same small set of details.
<v Vauhini Vara>在这里，我应该为你召唤我的姐姐。在这里，我应该描述她，以便你感受到我所感受的她的缺席，以便你也因此变得像个幽灵。但虽然我是作家，但我从未能召唤她。我记得的还是那几小条细节。

00:22:00.110 --> 00:22:11.580
<v Tobin Low>She stops there. "I remember the same small set of details," colon, blank space. It's a prompt meant to see what GPT-3 will say. Here's how it responds.
<v Tobin Low>她停在那儿。“我记得的还是那几小条细节”，冒号，空白处。这是一个旨在看看GPT-3会说什么的提示语。这是它的回应。

00:22:11.580 --> 00:22:37.110
<v GPT-3>Her dark eyes, her long, thin fingers-- but these are just the details that are universal to all sisters. If I describe the color of her eyes and the shape of her fingers, you might think that I was describing someone else. Even if you knew my sister, you might not recognize her in these details. Why is it that though we look at our siblings so closely, we forget them so quickly?
<v GPT-3>她深色的眼睛，她又长又细的手指——但这只是所有姐妹共有的细节。如果你描述她眼睛的颜色和手指的形状，你可能会认为我描述的是别人。即使你认识我姐姐，你也可能认不出这些细节中的她。为什么虽然我们如此仔细地看着我们的兄弟姐妹，但我们却这么快就忘记了他们？

00:22:37.110 --> 00:23:02.250
<v GPT-3>So I can't describe her to you, but I can describe what it felt like to have her die. It felt like my life was an accident, or worse, a mistake. I'd made a mistake in being born. And now, to correct it, I would have to die. I'd have to die and someone else, a stranger, would have to live in my place. I was that stranger. I still am.
<v GPT-3>所以我不能为你描述她，但我可以描述我姐姐去世时的感觉。感觉我的生活是一场意外，或者更糟，一个错误。我出生就是一个错误。而现在，为了纠正它，我必须死。我必须死，然后别人，一个陌生人，将代替我生活。我就是那个陌生人。我现在依然是。

00:23:02.250 --> 00:23:06.570
<v Tobin  Low>What do you think about what it filled in your prompt with?
