00:23:06.570 --> 00:23:25.190
<v Vauhini  Vara>She did have dark eyes. And weirdly, she did have long, thin fingers. And again, I want to say, I don't know how it knew that. Of course, it's not-- it doesn't have consciousness. But it did get those two things right.
<v Vauhini  Vara>她确实有深色的眼睛。奇怪的是，她确实有又长又细的手指。我还是要再说一次，我不知道它是怎么知道的。当然，它不是——它没有意识。但它确实说对了那两点。

00:23:25.190 --> 00:23:48.650
<v Tobin Low>The rest of it, about wanting to die, feeling like a mistake, it felt a little extreme. But seeing the computer's sort of clumsy attempt to describe her sister, it gave her something to react to. Like, seeing the software do it badly made her realize how to do it better. So in version six, she tries to do the thing that was so hard, writing about her sister herself. Here's what she writes.
<v Tobin Low>剩下的部分，关于想死、感觉像个错误，感觉有点极端。但看到电脑笨拙地试图描述她姐姐，它给了她一些可以反应的东西。就像，看到软件做得不好，让她意识到该如何做得更好。所以在第六个版本中，她试着做那件最难的事情，自己写关于姐姐的内容。这是她写的。

00:23:48.650 --> 00:24:07.990
<v Vauhini Vara>"I remember the same small set of details-- her loud laugh, her bossiness and swagger, her self-consciousness about her broad nose, her curly hair. But even this isn't fixed. Her hair fell out. Her nose narrowed. She began moving slowly and carefully.
<v Vauhini Vara>“我记得的还是那几小条细节——她响亮的笑声、她的专横和招摇、她对自己大鼻子的自我意识、她卷曲的头发。但即使这些也不是固定的。她的头发掉了。她的鼻子变窄了。她开始移动得很慢、很小心。

00:24:07.990 --> 00:24:19.320
<v Vauhini Vara>We'd go down to Clark Beach that spring that she was dying. She wanted to show us where to spread her ashes. And when we'd walk back up, I'd have to put a hand on the small of her back and push her. She did not laugh as often."
<v Vauhini Vara>在她垂死的那年春天，我们去过克拉克海滩。她想告诉我们把她的骨灰撒在哪里。当我们走回来时，我不得不把手放在她的后腰上推她。她不再频繁地大笑了。”

00:24:19.320 --> 00:24:34.200
<v Tobin Low>It's in this version in the next that Vauhini and GPT-3 start to feel like they're talking to each other, trading stories about the little moments that happen between sisters. Like, GPT-3 makes up the scene where Vauhini and her sister are kids in their childhood home.
<v Tobin Low>正是在这个版本和下一个版本中，沃希尼和GPT-3开始觉得他们正在交谈，交换着发生在姐妹之间的小时刻。比如，GPT-3编造了一个场景，沃希尼和她姐姐小时候在她们的童年家里。

00:24:34.200 --> 00:24:44.580
<v GPT-3>I heard her calling my name from the living room. "What?" I said. "I'm awake," she called back. "Are you?" I said. "Yes," she said. "I'm awake."
